  "notes": "Every client-addressable requirement has exactly one disposition. A lane is produced when the nightly (nightly-certification.yml) dispatches the named workflow at the candidate it resolved; its source revision is the catalog's source_revisions[source_revision_key]. Input values are literal strings or one of {server_image}, {server_sha}, {cut_at} from the resolved candidate. An unproduced lane has no producer the nightly can bind to a candidate: it stays a skip in the ledger, the gate refuses it at its required tier, and its owner cuts the producer named in missing_producer. Non-addressable requirements need no producer and are counted separately. A disposition selects requirements by client_lanes (glob) or deployment_targets; deployment_targets keeps desktop-client lanes unnamed in this public repository (R30).",
